// `check_let_ann` sends an int literal to a FIT check, and that check returns
// early when the annotation is not integer-like - so the type comparison never
// ran. A branch standing in for another has to say when it does not apply and
// hand over.
//
// The helper that recognises the literal folds a negation and a cast, so `-1`
// and `1 as int` arrive by the same door: the hole was wider than the literal it
// was named after.
fn main() { let x: bool = 1; println(if x { 1 } else { 0 }); }
